From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: reserve the stock XBL/AOP gap

The HD1913 stock device tree reserves 0x85e00000-0x85f40000 as one
XBL/AOP region. The generic SM8150 description instead reserves XBL at
0x85d00000-0x85e40000 and AOP plus cmd-db at
0x85f00000-0x85f40000. This leaves 0x85e40000-0x85f00000 available to
Linux on hotdog even though the device firmware still owns it.

A full DDR capture after a reproducible Qualcomm crashdump found two
Flatpak page-cache folios covering that entire 768 KiB hole. Reserve the
missing portion as no-map so the page allocator cannot reuse firmware
memory under pressure.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ / {
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		xbl_aop_gap: memory@85e40000 {
+			reg = <0 0x85e40000 0 0xc0000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		hotdog_removed_gap: hotdog-removed-gap@89d00000 {
 			reg = <0 0x89d00000 0 0x1a00000>;
 			no-map;
-- 
2.50.1
